<html lang="en" class="oci-theme">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<title>Model and GPU discovery · OKE model serving</title>
<style>${theme_css}</style>
</head>
<body>
<header class="oci-header"><span class="oci-header__brand">OKE model serving</span><span class="oci-caption">Model &amp; GPU discovery</span></header>
<main>
<div class="oci-page-heading"><div class="page-width"><p class="eyebrow">Deployment assessment</p><h1 id="model-title" class="oci-page-title">Model discovery</h1><p id="report-subtitle"></p><p id="report-time" class="oci-caption"></p></div></div>
<div class="oci-stripe" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="oci-workspace page-width">
<noscript><p>This report needs JavaScript to display its embedded discovery data. No additional discovery requests are made when the page opens.</p></noscript>
<nav class="section-nav" aria-label="Report sections"><a class="oci-link" href="#model-information">Model information</a><a class="oci-link" href="#memory-requirements">Memory requirements</a><a class="oci-link" href="#deployment-options">Deployment options</a><a class="oci-link" href="#regional-capacity">Regional GPU capacity</a></nav>
<section id="model-information" aria-labelledby="model-heading"><h2 id="model-heading">Model information</h2><div id="model-links" class="oci-toolbar"></div><dl id="model-details" class="facts"></dl><p id="model-provenance" class="muted oci-caption"></p></section>
<section id="memory-requirements" aria-labelledby="memory-heading"><h2 id="memory-heading">Memory requirements</h2><p id="workload"></p><div id="memory-metrics" class="metrics"></div><div id="memory-status"></div><p id="memory-assumptions" class="muted"></p></section>
<section id="deployment-options" aria-labelledby="options-heading"><div class="section-heading"><h2 id="options-heading">Deployment options</h2><span id="option-count" class="oci-caption" aria-live="polite"></span></div>
<p>Compare serving layouts using the same regional capacity scan. Each option targets one AD and checks physical supply and entitlement for its complete host allocation. Expand an option to review its role counts, configuration and deployment links.</p>
<details class="recipe-details configuration-guide"><summary>How serving configurations use GPUs and caches</summary>
<dl class="facts">
<div><dt>Tensor parallelism (TP)</dt><dd>Shards one model instance across GPUs. Each P/D role has its own TP group.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Pipeline parallelism (PP)</dt><dd>Splits model layers into stages. Combined serving can use supported TP/PP layouts; the current P/D adapter requires PP=1.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Replicas</dt><dd>Independent model instances, each holding a complete set of weights across its GPUs. Spare GPU slots on allocated hosts can hold extra complete instances.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Combined prefill + decode</dt><dd>Each serving instance processes the input prompt and generates the output tokens.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Separate prefill / decode (P/D)</dt><dd>Prefill processes the prompt and transfers its KV state to decode, which generates output tokens. Both roles hold the full model weights, sharded across their own GPUs.</dd></div>
<div><dt>P/D GPU demand</dt><dd>One prefill plus one decode at the same TP needs twice the GPUs of one combined instance. It does not always double an existing replicated fleet: roles may share spare slots on a host. The cards show actual role counts and whole-host allocation.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Prefix caching</dt><dd>Reuses previously computed KV state for matching prompt prefixes inside a serving engine.</dd></div>
<div><dt>Prefix-aware routing</dt><dd>Uses request affinity to encourage prefix reuse. It does not inspect actual KV cache residency.</dd></div>
<div><dt>KV-aware routing</dt><dd>Routes using actual cache residency. It is unavailable in the current router integration. P/D transfer and engine prefix caching can work without it.</dd></div>
</dl>
<p>MoE models can support P/D. Eligibility depends on the attention/cache layout, serving image and connector; an MoE model still needs its resident expert weights. The current P/D adapter offers known text-only uniform-attention layouts, fixed role counts, one host per role instance, matching TP and unquantized KV cache, with LMCache disabled. Other layouts remain unavailable until assessed.</p>
<p class="muted">Eligibility is permission to test, not proof of runtime support or a speedup. Deployment checks serving and observes KV transfer, recomputation or missing evidence. Benchmarks compare workloads separately.</p>
</details>
<div id="failures"></div>
<div id="layout-tabs" class="layout-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Serving layout">
<button id="layout-tab-aggregated" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="layout-panel" tabindex="0">Combined prefill + decode</button>
<button id="layout-tab-disaggregated" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="layout-panel" tabindex="-1">Separate prefill / decode (P/D)</button>
</div>
<div id="layout-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="layout-tab-aggregated" tabindex="0">
<p id="layout-description"></p><div id="layout-status" aria-live="polite"></div>
<div class="filters"><label>Filter options<input id="search" type="search" placeholder="Region, shape or availability domain"></label><label>Sort options<select id="sort"><option value="region">Region, shape and AD</option><option value="allocated">Fewest allocated GPUs</option><option value="capacity">Most available GPUs in AD</option></select></label></div><p id="recommendation-policy" class="muted"></p><div id="options" class="options"></div><p id="option-empty" class="muted" hidden>No matching deployment options.</p>
</div></section>
<section id="regional-capacity" aria-labelledby="capacity-heading"><h2 id="capacity-heading">Regional GPU capacity and limits</h2><p>Physical supply below is listed separately for each AD, never pooled across ADs for a node pool. Configured limits and remaining compartment headroom retain their OCI scope; regional/global ceilings are shared, not additive. Only positive reported host capacity is listed; zero and unconfirmed-only observations are excluded from deployment choices. Physical capacity and entitlement are separate checks. Red values are below the whole-host GPU allocation needed for the model; unknown sizing or quota units are not treated as confirmed shortages. A limit increase can help only where hardware is reported available; model layout and runtime compatibility still need validation.</p><div class="filters"><label>Filter capacity<input id="capacity-search" type="search" placeholder="Region, AD or GPU shape"></label></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><caption class="sr-only">Capacity by region, availability domain and exact GPU shape; alternative shapes may share supply.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Region / AD / GPU shape</th><th scope="col">GPUs needed</th><th scope="col">GPUs per host</th><th scope="col">Current limit and headroom</th><th scope="col">Physical capacity per AD</th><th scope="col">Entitlement and model sizing</th></tr></thead><tbody id="capacity"></tbody></table></div><p id="capacity-empty" class="muted" hidden>No matching capacity observations.</p></section>
<section aria-labelledby="notes-heading"><h2 id="notes-heading">Assessment notes</h2><ul id="notices" class="muted"></ul></section>
</div>
</main>
<footer class="oci-footer"><span>OKE model serving · Discovery report</span><span>Capacity is a snapshot, not a reservation.</span></footer>
<script id="report-data" type="application/json">${report_json}</script>
<script>${report_script}</script>
</body></html>
